{
  "category": "Caring Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "The special membrane enveloping Alomomola has the ability to heal wounds.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Floating in the open sea is how they live. When they find a wounded Pokémon, they embrace it and bring it to shore.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "It gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Floating in the open sea is how they live. When they find a wounded Pokémon, they embrace it and bring it to shore.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "It gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Floating in the open sea is how they live. When they find a wounded Pokémon, they embrace it and bring it to shore.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "It gently holds injured and weak Pokémon in its fins. Its special membrane heals their wounds.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses its special mucus to close the wounds of injured Pokémon. The reason for this behavior remains unknown.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "They float upon the open sea. Many water Pokémon gather in the area around Alomomola.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fishermen take them along on long voyages, because if you have an Alomomola with you, there’ll be no need for a doctor or medicine.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "The reason it helps Pokémon in a weakened condition is that any Pokémon coming after them may also attack Alomomola.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    }
  ],
